{#
  The site's one "let the AI do this field for me" button: a magic wand,
  no text (design.md §7.4's icon vocabulary).

  It exists because « Générer avec l'IA » next to an input is wider than
  most phones can spare — on the article editor the summary field, the
  one that actually needs the room, was squeezed to a few characters by
  the button beside it. The four buttons that carried that kind of label
  (« Générer avec l'IA » twice, « Raccourcir avec l'IA »,
  « Expliquer avec l'IA ») now all render the same way, so the wand means
  the same thing everywhere it appears.

  The wording never disappears: it becomes `title` (hover) and
  `aria-label` (screen readers), which is what makes an icon-only control
  legitimate rather than a guessing game.

  This is for a helper attached to a field or a result. A page-level
  primary action that happens to call an AI (« Générer le contenu » on
  the RGPD page) is not one of these and keeps its label.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/ai_button.html.twig' with {
      id: 'news-ai-summary-btn',
      label: "Générer avec l'IA",   -- title + aria-label, always French
      variant: 'outline-secondary', -- optional, default outline-secondary
      size: 'sm',                   -- optional, '' for the default size
      class_extra: 'd-none',        -- optional
      disabled: true,               -- optional
      data: { 'shorten-btn': '' },  -- optional data-* attributes
  } only %}
#}
<button type="button"
        class="btn btn-{{ variant|default('outline-secondary') }}{{ size|default('') ? ' btn-' ~ size : '' }}{{ class_extra|default('') ? ' ' ~ class_extra : '' }}"
        {%- if id|default('') %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}
        {%- if disabled|default(false) %} disabled{% endif %}
        {%- for key, value in data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %}
        title="{{ label }}" aria-label="{{ label }}">
    <i class="bi bi-magic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>
